  "enable": "NetworkCtrl (MV 24562, \"Network source\", 1 = Off / 2 = On) is the writable on/off object; ActOpSta (MV 32321) reports 11 = BMS when the network is in control. Summer/winter follows the BMS only when SuWiChgSrc (MV 9493) = 3 (BMS); then write SuWiNetworkChgover (MV 28594). The guide gives no further procedure.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet IP comes from a POL908 module and BACnet MS/TP from a POL904 module plugged onto the MicroTech controller.",
   "BACnet MS/TP module defaults: MAC address 24, 38400 baud, Max Master 127, Max Info Frames 1; cycle power after changing the address.",
   "Object instances are fixed, non-sequential numbers (e.g. SupplyTmp = AI 45150); map by instance, not by position."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Objects only appear when the AHU configuration uses them (fans, coils, recovery, humidity, ERQ units).",
   "Fan setpoint units follow SplyEngUnit / ExhEngUnit (%, Pa or m3/h); humidity units follow HumEngUnit.",
   "Multistate commands are 1-based (1 = Off, 2 = On); 0 is not a valid state.",
   "AckAlmPls (MV 39130) acknowledges every alarm in the controller at once.",
   "EmergencyStop (BI 9864) reads 0 = Alarm, 1 = OK, the reverse of the other alarm inputs."
  ]
